ction; (5) **Psychiatric symptoms** — depression, apathy, pseudobulbar affect. MRI shows **extensive white matter hyperintensities** with **characteristic involvement of the anterior temporal poles and external capsules** (a finding highly suggestive of CADASIL). Diagnosis is confirmed by NOTCH3 gene testing or skin biopsy showing granular osmiophilic material (GOM) in vessel walls. (Ref: Hazzard''''s Ch. 72; Current D&T Geriatrics)'),
