 (5) **Sialorrhea** (drooling). Management of orthostatic hypotension includes: compression stockings, increased salt/fluid intake, elevating head of bed, and if needed, **midodrine** or **droxidopa** (FDA-approved for neurogenic OH). Fludrocortisone is second-line. (Ref: Hazzard''''s Ch. 72; AGS Geriatrics At Your Fingertips)'),
